  "worked_solution": "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0+0+0 & 3+0+0 & 6+0+0 \\\\ 0+6+4 & -1-4+0 & -2+0+12 \\\\ 0+15-2 & 0-10+0 & 0+0-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 13 & -10 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
